    modelAnswer: 'I would say: "{p3}, I hear you: the pour is at six, 40,000 is on the line and this lands on you. I am going to try to get you steel for the pour." Then the honest part: I cannot send a load tonight. My driver is out of legal hours and the only other vehicle cannot unload steel safely on your site; a crew unloading by hand is how people get hurt, and I will not do that to your team or mine. Then the resolution: I will call our sister branch and two crane contractors now and aim for a certified delivery on site at 5am. "I will call you back by 5pm today with a yes or no and a time." If it fails, I would help {p3} find a supplier who can. Afterwards I would suggest an early warning arrangement for pours so we do not meet like this again.',
